  <h2>How a gift-card redemption works</h2>
  <ul class="tick-list">
    <li class="good"><b>Compare minimums.</b> A lower gift-card threshold may make a smaller balance redeemable, subject to the remaining conditions.</li>
    <li class="good"><b>Same verification.</b> First redemptions still require identity checks before the operator releases the prize.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Not cash.</b> A gift card is locked to a retailer or card network and cannot be deposited like a bank transfer.</li>
    <li class="bad"><b>Retailer fit.</b> Value depends on whether you would shop at the offered retailer anyway.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Gift card vs other rails</h2>
  <p>Compare a gift card's spending restrictions with a <a href="/guides/redemption-methods/bank-transfer/">bank transfer</a> or the wallet requirements of <a href="/guides/redemption-methods/crypto/">cryptocurrency</a>. A lower minimum does not establish faster delivery. See the <a href="/guides/sweepstakes-casino-redemption-methods/">redemption methods guide</a> for the operator records.</p>

